---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';

const MY_MAPS = 'https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?usp=sharing&mid=';

// Index + 1 is the area number.
const areaMapIds = [
	'10ecWSiC07oALogVr_baKvskXwpQdyfE',
	'1enQBzYKVZTySfLHPphz6EhhWVujfoss',
	'13hH9VLNBGSvLdYalVAxLvYP5jL058wY',
	'1DH2LGAjB6Oa6-xsbBfq_wzv6BzkHEZY',
	'1ZGN73_t7Gq_w28XgJmN9sQNvWPdUTY8',
	'1_zoFSpMgM6gl4AuzFNXd4VdSq_35Pp4',
	'19DhWOMxmF_1mG-zYCkub9cN81Vh6LxQ',
	'1dn-8cMxvkS9SQ0nwqqHjqKUx-107ikI',
	'1OCXUWF4jZ9mjR70Jgz0fIxfp9Zh5A2A',
	'1HC_8FguPCkbglI_UQPt_almchKqLL9I',
	'1gkc962ohDA3SjsSzBMul6leFT-mY7bQ',
	'1NUuUvVqMG0N6J7e-yGl6UkW7KTLPzME',
	'1SzJTtjElodIiRbflS6c9YuopI4L0L-Y',
	'1x1Dzcw5okkvFFokRrPhzvnUK4eTYQe8',
	'1EF7LH2lreCPLqg5JIJLwyQpJ6w-TaGM',
	'1bNTVPnu1eCqBZpOs0UzuJSSR6SzKzBY',
	'1gmANq8qexNVyAuQK_2hDStr1l8jAfCY',
	'1Jyj4w1YhC9K1CfMCrBTf53_G4wgUTEA',
	'1CLXYHBhYySV94cODDVHr_JgrE4CzqBA',
	'1tbLl7FKBFLKHlkLs_ixfRh0t5O1TqEE',
	'1YuBun5BwYZocJ3kGKtPcWNdA27r-qAs',
	'1m-FbyCmvc-LgBep0b3sh5PA9n0wLzE0',
	'17a8l_Fm0UE7wOQFCck0ZmOJoFky_6UA',
	'14d0O5-zs2Mfxl4hdRgcI4HqYeYusQa4',
] as const;

const areas = areaMapIds.map((id, index) => ({ label: `Area #${index + 1} Map`, href: MY_MAPS + id }));
const half = Math.ceil(areas.length / 2);
const leftColumn = areas.slice(0, half);
const rightColumn = areas.slice(half);
---

<Page title="Count Circle Maps" wide>
	<p>
		The Bloomington count circle is centered at the intersection of Hwy 77 and Hwy 13 (latitude: 44.8127, longitude:
		-93.2199). It is a very complex circle, divided into 24 areas. (Note that as of 2024, we have divided Areas 1, 2, 3,
		and 20 in half to create 4 new areas.)
	</p>
	<p>
		Below are Google Maps for the entire count circle. You can use them for reference, and use while counting and keep
		track of where you are in your count area using Google Maps. To use them on your phone, open an individual area map on
		your phone, and it should bring up in Google Maps. <a href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1MiNkOi9EYoEUPBSr-2HbV_SZ5tvjQHt1?usp=sharing">Printable PDF versions</a> of these maps are also available to download. To see a full screen view, click on the [ ] icon on the top right.
	</p>
	<p>
		Scroll down the page to see eBird sightings and hotspots superimposed on our count circle map. If you're curious how
		I got that data, see my code at <a href="https://github.com/lizmstanley/cbc_utils">https://github.com/lizmstanley/cbc_utils</a> (yes, I'm a software engineer.)
	</p>

	<div class="circle-maps">
		<ul class="area-links">
			{leftColumn.map((area) => <li><a class="button-link" href={area.href}>{area.label}</a></li>)}
		</ul>
		<iframe
			class="circle-map"
			src="https://www.google.com/maps/d/embed?mid=1LQTekqLvDBMRHiXegW45hZ1tiPSYRlo"
			title="Bloomington count circle with all 24 areas"
			loading="lazy"></iframe>
		<ul class="area-links">
			{rightColumn.map((area) => <li><a class="button-link" href={area.href}>{area.label}</a></li>)}
		</ul>
	</div>

	<hr />

	<p>
		This area map shows recent eBird sightings that have been reported within the count circle in the last 7 days. It
		includes different layers for notable, confirmed and provisional sightings. Click on the [ ] icon on the top right to
		open a full screen view, and select different layers to switch between them (for example to filter out provisional
		sightings.)
	</p>
	<iframe
		src="https://www.google.com/maps/d/embed?mid=1p4yoPyQc1XeRrQMjABiijS8-1eIbZU0"
		title="Recent eBird sightings in the count circle"
		height="680"
		loading="lazy"></iframe>

	<hr />

	<p>
		This map shows all the eBird hotspots within our count circle. These are good locations to find birds! Click on the [ ]
		icon on the right to open up a full screen view of the map.
	</p>
	<iframe
		src="https://www.google.com/maps/d/embed?mid=14BF5L25-m4XHydXibYoarC-26BJpZHI"
		title="eBird hotspots in the count circle"
		height="680"
		loading="lazy"></iframe>
</Page>

<style>
	.circle-maps {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 11rem 1fr 11rem;
		gap: 1.75rem;
		align-items: start;
		margin: 2rem 0;
	}

	.area-links {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.9rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.area-links li {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.circle-maps .circle-map {
		height: 660px;
		margin: 0;
	}

	@media (max-width: 820px) {
		.circle-maps {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		}

		.circle-maps .circle-map {
			grid-column: 1 / -1;
			grid-row: 1;
			height: 480px;
		}
	}
</style>
